  {
    "code": "octgn:8bc0199c-09ff-463f-a6b5-886d14d843cc",
    "octgnid": "8bc0199c-09ff-463f-a6b5-886d14d843cc",
    "name": "The Siege of Annúminas",
    "type_code": "rules",
    "sphere_code": "encounter",
    "traits": "",
    "text": "Setting Up Epic Multiplayer Mode\nThe Setup instructions on the epic multiplayer mode setup card instruct the players to create 3 separate staging areas with 3 different quest decks. To do this, take the quest cards from a single copy of The Siege of Annúminas and arrange them into 3 separate quest decks: 1A–3A, 1C–3C, and 1E–3E. Remove the unused quest cards from the event.\nNext, the players divide themselves into 3 teams, one team for each stage. At least 1 player must be assigned to each stage, and no more than 4 players can be assigned to a single stage.\nOnly 1 copy of the epic multiplayer mode setup card should be used by the group while setting up the game. After completing the Setup instructions, flip over all 3 Setup cards and place 1 next to each quest deck.",
    "is_unique": false,
    "pack_code": "TSoA",
    "pack_name": "The Siege of Annúminas",
    "position": 998,
    "quantity": 0,
    "encounter_set": "The Siege of Annuminas",
    "back_name": "The Siege of Annúminas",
    "back_text": "Playing Epic Multiplayer Mode\nThe players at each stage are the only players in the game at that stage. That means it is possible for two players at different stages to use the same hero. However, players at the same stage must observe the game restrictions on unique cards. Player cards cannot target or affect cards at a different stage.\nWhen a team ends a round at their stage they do not advance to the next round of play until each other team in that group is ready to advance. Furthermore, abilities that trigger at the end of the round resolve in alphabetical stage order. (Resolve end of round effects at stage 2B before resolving end of round effects at stage 2D, etc.)\nImmune to Player Card Effects\nCards with the text \"Immune to player card effects\" ignore the effects of all player cards. Additionally, cards that are immune to player card effects cannot be chosen as targets of player card effects.",
    "back_type_code": "rules",
    "back_imagesrc": "/cards/8bc0199c-09ff-463f-a6b5-886d14d843cc.B.jpg",
    "printed_stats": {},
    "imagesrc": "/cards/8bc0199c-09ff-463f-a6b5-886d14d843cc.jpg",
    "packs": [
      {
        "pack_code": "TSoA",
        "pack_name": "The Siege of Annúminas",
        "position": 998,
        "quantity": 0,
        "octgnid": "8bc0199c-09ff-463f-a6b5-886d14d843cc",
        "imagesrc": "https://dragncards-lotrlcg.s3.amazonaws.com/cards/English/8bc0199c-09ff-463f-a6b5-886d14d843cc.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "source": "dragncards",
